This character started about 6 months ago, shortly after my first
great Valkyrie got brainsucked. Potions of extra healing turned out to
be smoky, though she only ever got 1 wish from one. She played for a
while, clearing out the Mines with a pet red dragon (which she
abandoned), the Quest, and finally the Castle. She had a minor mishap
at Medusa, where a nearby titan summoned a large pack of nasties
(including 2 master mind flayers), so she quickly dug downward to the
castle.  After clearing out the castle, she used up the wand (started
at 0:1) on 2 charging scrolls, a magic marker (for enchanting armor),
SDSM, speed boots, and 2 scrolls of genocide (with which she quickly
genocided L and h). A lich had destroyed her earlier armor, so that
was all she was wearing at the time. At this point, her weapons were
very good (+6 Mojo and silver saber), but her AC of -11 left much to
be desired.  At this point, I saved her to disk and filed her away.

Six months later...

I dropped down into the Valley and quickly cleared it out. By the
priest, I decided to bless and drink a few potions of extra healing
and the first one gave me a wish. Blessed fireproof +2 cloak of magic
resistance, please. Now confident that I could survive Gehennom, I
descended and cleared the first few levels. Shortly afterwards, I got
bored and decided I would try this new thing called "pudding farming",
so I ran through the dungeons to find a level with both an altar and a
sink. Thousands of turns later (with teleportitis from an ungrateful
tengu by now), the entire level was dug out and a swarm of puddings
was flowing about. Unfortunately, uncontrolled teleportitis made the
farming (with a nice dull knife) rather difficult (managed to get
crowned and get a few spellbooks), so I cleared out Gehennom (bribing
Asmodeus and Baalzebub), marking the vibrating square and finding Vlad
on the way up.

Back to my pudding farm, I did some limited farming and got some
rings, one of which I managed to polypile into teleport control.
Overjoyed, I put it on. Over the next 30K turns or so, I farmed
puddings to get massive piles of scrolls, potions, wands, spellbooks,
and worthless pieces of glass. Unwanted items were polypiled into
useful ones - 5 amulets of life saving (of the 2 remaining, one from
Vlad and another from a dumb monster), 60+ ID scrolls, 20+ enchant
armor scrolls, enough potions to max my stats and get me to level 30
and >600HP, and several pages worth of spellbooks. Several gauntlets
of power turned up while polypiling, but I declined (wanted to be able
to cast spells) in favor of gauntlets of dexterity (which I never
found), so I settled with leather. No helm of brilliance ever showed
itself to me, so I settled with an elven leather helm. Liberal usage
of the Drain Life spell got my equipment all to +5/+7 (and
disenchanters were genocided in order to keep it this way).

Satisfied (with an AC of -50, rings of slow digestion + free action +
levitation + regeneration + conflict, and all my spells refreshed), I
decided to get it over with and start my ascension run. Invoking the
Orb quickly took me to the portal to Rodney's tower (which I had
cleared out in advance), and Rodney died in a few hits (after dodging
2 death rays). Running quickly to the Sanctum (and meeting Rodney
twice on the way), I performed the invocation and proceeded to empty
out the Sanctum (and light the area around the altar for my
convenience). A few smacks later, the high priest gave me the Amulet
(which I promptly named).

Escaping from Gehennom was only mildly problematic, feeling the Force
7 times. Rodney showed up 3 times along the way, dying to 2 death rays
and one severe beating. Finally, I reached level 1 and ascended to the
Plane of Earth...

Here, Rodney made his final appearance and learned just how powerful
Mjollnir and a silver saber can be. By now, one spell had gone
twisted, so I used this to my advantage and located the portal. Two
digging zaps later, I arrived on the Plane of Air and put on my ring
of levitation. Only a few air elementals actually managed to swallow
me, and they were dispatched rather quickly (apparently, AC -50 really
DOES make a difference over -38). I eagerly stepped onto the Plane of
Fire, located the portal, and made a mad dash for it, killing 2
Archons on the way (leaving a 3rd one behind) before they could manage
to initiate a summoning storm. Dropping into a bubble in the Plane of
Water, I located the portal and then floated in its general direction,
dodging the eels and krakens (which I had neglected to genocide) and
finally landed on the Astral Plane.

My guardian angel appeared, and I started toward the central altar
(guarded by Death). I killed every hostile @ in sight and entered the
high temple, only to find out it was Chaotic. Annoyed, I tried the
left altar next (guarded by Famine, where I nearly had a close call by
getting weak before I could chow down some K-rations). On the way, an
NPC gave me the +4 Frost Brand and a priest gave me a magic marker.
Entering the temple, it was Lawful. Even more annoyed than before
(since I had started on the right side of the entrance area), I
proceeded to the right. On the way, I found a figurine of an Aleax.
Amused, I applied it and it turned out tame. Even more amused, I
continued onward, killing Pestilence a few times on the way. When I
finally reached the altar, I breathed a sigh of relief and offered the
amulet.

Not bad for my first 'local' ascension (my first two were played on
nethack.alt.org), considering it started before my first ascension was
completed. Now I finally have an ascension in my own local high score
list. :)

